WEBVTT

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:10.190
<b>Are You Lost?</b>

00:00:10.190 --> 00:00:12.990
<b>Are You Lost?</b>

00:01:05.490 --> 00:01:08.000
Everyone must be on summer vacation now.

00:01:08.490 --> 00:01:11.630
Oh, yeah... You're right.

00:01:11.630 --> 00:01:15.550
<b>We Will Rescue Her</b>

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:15.550
I wish I could've been
in it... the inter-high...

00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:21.930
Not that there's any point
thinking about that now—

00:01:21.930 --> 00:01:25.100
Shion!

00:01:40.050 --> 00:01:41.580
What's wrong, Homare?!

00:01:41.860 --> 00:01:43.660
Did something happen?

00:01:47.310 --> 00:01:49.940
It's Shion... I can't see her.

00:01:50.530 --> 00:01:52.380
She might have been swept away.

00:01:55.320 --> 00:01:57.220
"Might have been"?

00:01:57.220 --> 00:01:58.970
What's that supposed to mean?

00:02:00.750 --> 00:02:03.060
What do you mean?

00:02:04.060 --> 00:02:08.140
What were you doing, Homare?
You were with her, weren't you?

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:11.810
I'm sorry.

00:02:13.060 --> 00:02:15.480
Asuka-san! Calm down!

00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:21.570
Not much time has elapsed.

00:02:22.130 --> 00:02:24.030
I'll make a raft and go after her.

00:02:24.030 --> 00:02:26.500
Help me. Every second counts.

00:02:33.210 --> 00:02:35.590
<i>Homare. Listen carefully.</i>

00:02:36.500 --> 00:02:39.930
In harsh survival conditions,
your first priority will always be...

00:02:40.540 --> 00:02:42.610
your own life.

00:02:43.340 --> 00:02:47.500
Even if there are others with you,
you should not take risks.

00:02:48.160 --> 00:02:49.990
Kindness can cost you your life.

00:02:51.260 --> 00:02:54.420
<i>Think about your own safety first.</i>

00:02:57.300 --> 00:02:59.040
<i>I'm sorry, Papa.</i>

00:02:59.610 --> 00:03:02.620
<b>Are You Lost?</b>

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:05.450
Ready, Homare? We'll push you out.

00:03:05.450 --> 00:03:06.740
Yes. Thanks.

00:03:06.740 --> 00:03:08.590
Ready, and...

00:03:09.070 --> 00:03:12.560
<i>When I stand on the raft,
my eye line is about 160 cm.</i>

00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:15.090
<i>The furthest I can see is
four to five kilometers.</i>

00:03:15.720 --> 00:03:20.860
<i>Even if I manage to catch the same current,
my chances of finding Shion are low.</i>

00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:22.840
<i>But still...</i>

00:03:22.840 --> 00:03:24.430
Homare!

00:03:27.640 --> 00:03:30.500
You'll bring Shion back, right?

00:03:30.500 --> 00:03:32.390
Please, Homare-san!

00:03:34.650 --> 00:03:35.870
Don't worry.

00:03:36.540 --> 00:03:37.960
I will save her!

00:03:56.530 --> 00:03:58.750
This can't be real!

00:03:58.750 --> 00:04:03.680
Where am I? Why am I here?

00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:05.840
<i>Humans cannot live without water.</i>

00:04:06.540 --> 00:04:09.280
Two liters a day is the basic requirement,

00:04:09.280 --> 00:04:12.390
but depending on circumstances,
more might be necessary.

00:04:12.390 --> 00:04:15.200
That's why we have to stay
calm even in a crisis.

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:18.850
I can't cry.

00:04:18.850 --> 00:04:21.320
Tears are precious moisture.

00:04:25.810 --> 00:04:28.670
<i>I'm... thirsty...</i>

00:04:29.740 --> 00:04:31.580
<i>I managed to survive.</i>

00:04:31.580 --> 00:04:34.150
<i>I was even getting used
to living on the island, and now...</i>

00:04:34.820 --> 00:04:39.510
<i>I wonder if everyone's noticed I'm gone.</i>

00:04:40.440 --> 00:04:43.070
<i>To say goodbye like this...</i>

00:04:43.660 --> 00:04:46.000
<i>Everyone, stay safe until you get rescued.</i>

00:04:47.020 --> 00:04:50.140
<i>They're strong, so they'll be fine, right?</i>

00:04:51.180 --> 00:04:52.930
<i>I can't cry.</i>

00:04:52.930 --> 00:04:54.440
<i>I can't cry!</i>

00:04:58.770 --> 00:05:02.350
Is that... an island?

00:05:03.220 --> 00:05:05.030
If I can manage to get there...

00:05:05.030 --> 00:05:07.780
I might be able to survive!

00:05:21.210 --> 00:05:23.400
A-Asuka-san!

00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:24.260
Huh?

00:05:24.560 --> 00:05:28.530
Tonight, what if we steam the lily
bulbs and blanch the sea-spinach?

00:05:28.530 --> 00:05:30.890
And the main course'll be the
sole I caught this morning.

00:05:30.890 --> 00:05:31.560
Yes!

00:05:31.930 --> 00:05:36.350
I'm sure Shion-san and Homare-san
will be hungry when they come back.

00:05:36.350 --> 00:05:40.770
Let's get dinner ready
ourselves and surprise them.

00:05:40.770 --> 00:05:46.570
But what if Shion-san starts saying,
"I'd rather have had French cuisine"?

00:05:46.570 --> 00:05:48.420
We can't let her get away with being spoiled.

00:05:48.420 --> 00:05:49.700
No, we can't.

00:05:52.100 --> 00:05:55.370
They will come back, won't they? 
Both of them...

00:05:58.170 --> 00:06:00.460
You dummy. What're you talking about?

00:06:00.780 --> 00:06:05.170
It's Homare. Of course she's
gonna bring Shion back with her.

00:06:05.640 --> 00:06:07.470
She'll be fine!

00:06:09.020 --> 00:06:10.660
You're right.

00:06:10.660 --> 00:06:15.390
Homare-san has never failed
at anything she set out to do.

00:06:15.390 --> 00:06:16.310
Yeah.

00:06:16.840 --> 00:06:18.220
Come on. Let's head back.

00:06:18.220 --> 00:06:19.060
Okay!

00:06:20.270 --> 00:06:22.660
<i>Please, Homare.</i>

00:06:23.370 --> 00:06:26.600
<i>And Shion, hang in there 
until Homare finds you.</i>

00:06:31.420 --> 00:06:35.870
<i>This doesn't seem like
an island where people live.</i>

00:06:35.870 --> 00:06:36.700
Ow!

00:06:38.250 --> 00:06:42.000
<i>This seems more like
a big rock than an island.</i>

00:06:43.010 --> 00:06:45.270
<i>There aren't any trees or plants.</i>

00:06:46.220 --> 00:06:49.140
<i>I wonder if there could
be water in a place like this...</i>

00:06:49.970 --> 00:06:52.390
<i>Maybe I won't...</i>

00:06:53.910 --> 00:06:56.270
<i>No! I can't give up.</i>

00:07:06.560 --> 00:07:08.160
That was close.

00:07:12.950 --> 00:07:14.820
<i>A cave?</i>

00:07:14.820 --> 00:07:16.080
<i>Maybe there will be water here!</i>

00:07:17.420 --> 00:07:19.160
Huh? What's that?

00:07:20.020 --> 00:07:22.290
It's all squishy...

00:07:22.580 --> 00:07:24.880
<i>And it smells rotten.</i>

00:07:24.880 --> 00:07:29.060
No. I don't think there will
be drinkable water here.

00:07:31.160 --> 00:07:34.280
Water... I want a drink of water...

00:07:39.590 --> 00:07:42.820
<i>There's no food or water here.</i>

00:07:42.820 --> 00:07:46.120
<i>At this rate, it's only a matter
of time before I shrivel up.</i>

00:07:46.930 --> 00:07:50.550
<i>Even so, I don't know what to do...</i>

00:07:57.360 --> 00:08:00.460
<i>The current is probably moving
at about two to three km per hour.</i>

00:08:00.460 --> 00:08:04.290
<i>Since Shion was simply swept away,
I should be catching up to her about now, but...</i>

00:08:04.760 --> 00:08:07.130
<i>Could it be I've already passed her?</i>

00:08:11.430 --> 00:08:14.180
<i>My direction isn't precise,
it's only generally the same.</i>

00:08:14.180 --> 00:08:17.700
<i>If the sun sets, I won't
be able to look any more.</i>

00:08:18.100 --> 00:08:20.580
<i>I didn't have a concrete strategy...</i>

00:08:20.580 --> 00:08:22.600
<i>I just came out here in a panic.</i>

00:08:23.690 --> 00:08:26.950
Isn't there anything I can do?

00:08:28.500 --> 00:08:31.050
<i>It's too soon to give up, Homare.</i>

00:08:31.850 --> 00:08:34.740
But, I mean, we don't have
any tools or anything.

00:08:35.120 --> 00:08:39.500
I can't climb this tree. 
There's no way I can figure out how tall it is.

00:08:39.500 --> 00:08:43.020
There's no need to do that
to measure the height of the tree.

00:08:43.020 --> 00:08:43.660
Huh?

00:08:46.610 --> 00:08:51.320
From here, you and the tree are about
the same distance away from me.

00:08:51.320 --> 00:08:52.170
Okay!

00:08:52.170 --> 00:08:55.840
And the height of the tree is about
the same as your distance from the tree.

00:08:56.560 --> 00:08:57.580
Huh?

00:08:57.580 --> 00:08:58.470
Which means...

00:08:59.090 --> 00:09:03.100
If I figure out the distance from
the base of the tree to you, Homare,

00:09:03.880 --> 00:09:06.380
I will know how tall the tree is.

00:09:06.800 --> 00:09:09.220
This baobab is 22 meters tall.

00:09:09.220 --> 00:09:12.190
Oh! So I can figure it out like that!

00:09:12.540 --> 00:09:17.110
Homare, in survival conditions,
you need flexible thinking.

00:09:17.500 --> 00:09:21.160
No matter the circumstances,
there's always a way.

00:09:21.550 --> 00:09:23.590
You can't ever give up.

00:09:24.020 --> 00:09:27.080
Keep an open mind, and look
at things from every angle.

00:09:28.830 --> 00:09:30.840
<i>You're right, Papa.</i>

00:09:31.780 --> 00:09:35.150
<i>At my height, my field of vision
is at most four to five kilometers.</i>

00:09:35.150 --> 00:09:38.100
<i>But if I were higher up...</i>

00:09:38.100 --> 00:09:40.160
<i>I'd be able to see farther.</i>

00:09:48.600 --> 00:09:49.520
Okay.

00:09:49.520 --> 00:09:51.020
<i>If I can just...</i>

00:09:51.020 --> 00:09:52.570
<i>get a little higher!</i>

00:09:57.610 --> 00:09:58.360
<i>That's...</i>

00:10:14.680 --> 00:10:17.290
<i>Father. Mother.</i>

00:10:17.290 --> 00:10:19.300
<i>I've made some new friends.</i>

00:10:19.790 --> 00:10:20.840
<i>Asuka-san and...</i>

00:10:21.330 --> 00:10:22.430
<i>Mutsu-san and...</i>

00:10:22.820 --> 00:10:23.980
<i>and then there's...</i>

00:10:24.980 --> 00:10:27.140
<i>Homare-san.</i>

00:10:29.730 --> 00:10:33.580
<i>They're a little unusual,
but they are my very dear...</i>

00:10:38.190 --> 00:10:39.580
I'm so sorry.

00:10:40.750 --> 00:10:43.700
I just can't... go on...

00:10:44.910 --> 00:10:46.180
Yes, you can.

00:10:48.190 --> 00:10:49.010
Huh?

00:10:51.960 --> 00:10:54.570
How... are you here?

00:10:54.570 --> 00:10:58.540
No matter the circumstances,
there's always a way.

00:10:59.050 --> 00:11:01.150
I came to get you, Shion.

00:11:03.710 --> 00:11:05.150
Homare-san...

00:11:06.040 --> 00:11:08.890
You must have been scared. I'm sorry.

00:11:08.890 --> 00:11:10.730
Everything's all right now.

00:11:11.350 --> 00:11:12.060
Hey!

00:11:12.060 --> 00:11:14.650
What took you so long?

00:11:18.820 --> 00:11:21.070
Let's go home, Shion.

00:12:25.560 --> 00:12:29.450
Next time, Case 12:
 "How to Replenish Water."

00:12:28.010 --> 00:12:30.540
<b>How to Replenish Water</b>
